# =============================================================================
#  NEVER COMMIT — client data, project knowledge, models
#  This repository becomes public. Anything committed here is permanent:
#  forks propagate and GitHub caches. See docs/17-open-source-and-distribution.md
# =============================================================================

# Revit files — models, families, templates.
# Test models must be SYNTHETIC and go under tests/models/ (exception below).
*.rvt
*.rfa
*.rte
*.rft
*.rvt.*
*.0001.rvt
*.slog
*.dwg
*.dwf
*.nwc
*.nwd
*.ifc
!tests/models/**/*.rvt
!tests/models/**/*.rfa

# Source documents for ingestion — licensed standards and client-owned work.
# THE STORE WAS PROTECTED AND THE SOURCE WAS NOT. A knowledge store lives in
# %APPDATA%\Heron\knowledge and *.db is ignored below, so no ingested text can
# reach this repository. The PDF it was ingested FROM could, and that is the
# licensed half: NFPA and ASHRAE are bought per seat, QCS is somebody's
# publication, and a client specification is theirs. A fork propagates and
# GitHub caches, so this one is permanent if it happens once.
# Anything the repository genuinely needs is committed with an explicit
# exception, the way tests/models/ is above.
*.pdf
*.docx
*.doc
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.pptx
*.ppt

# Heron data class — belongs to the user, never to the repository
/workspace/
/data/
/Memory/
/Projects/
/Company/
/Community/
/Logs/
/Cache/
/Backup/
heron-workspace/
*.heron-db

# Knowledge stores and indexes (derived — rebuildable, never authoritative)
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.duckdb
*.lance
/vector-index/
/embeddings/

# Audit logs — contain project information
audit-*.jsonl
*.audit.jsonl

# Revit journals — contain file paths and project names
journal.*.txt
/journals/

