secrets.json
appsettings.Local.json
credentials.*

# =============================================================================
#  Build output
# =============================================================================

# .NET
bin/
obj/

# ...but NOT a skill's own bin/. `bin/` above is for .NET build output and it
# silently swallowed .claude/skills/heron-guard/bin/heron_guard.py - the hook
# the skill card advertises. The SKILL.md was committed, the executable it
# names was not, so every invocation of the hook would have failed before
# making a permission decision. Found by Codex on PR #44, 2026-09-09.
#
# The directory has to be re-included BEFORE the file: git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded.
!.claude/skills/*/bin/
!.claude/skills/*/bin/*.py
#
# The same trap nearly landed a second time: a copy of the skills briefly sat
# at .agents/skills/ and the re-include above did not follow it, so `bin/`
# swallowed heron_guard.py again at that path. Found 2026-09-10 before the
# first commit of it.
#
# That copy is GONE - the skills live at .claude/skills/ and nowhere else, and
# .codex/agents/*.toml points there too. These two lines are kept only as a
# tripwire: if anyone recreates .agents/skills/, the hook script comes with it
# instead of being silently dropped. Remove them once that risk is gone.
!.agents/skills/*/bin/
!.agents/skills/*/bin/*.py
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
.vs/
TestResults/
*.nupkg

